{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "reviewedScope": "On the delivered 614 bindless array-delta Core: DMA copies of R16G16B16A16Float and R32G32B32A32Float textures use the GPU-side copy for Hogwarts Legacy only (GraphicsConfig.HogwartsFloatDmaGpuCopy, set per session by the Library from the launched title; every other title keeps the MeloNX exclusion), into a block-linear destination with the same element size and a target sized in bytes; a destination texture that cannot be created falls back to the copy through guest memory (all formats). Every 2D copy still read through guest memory is attributed by bounded logging (each signature once, at most 8 per reason; counts per reason every 1024 copies, at most 32 times; no allocation per copy once full). Bindless delta passes skip the verification scan when no texture was invalidated during the pass (Texture.InvalidationEpoch) and visit only the pool ids logged since their last pass when that set is exact (TexturePool change log); otherwise the full scan or rebuild as before. The array-delta, fragmented-read (complete final GPU assembly), binding-snapshot and collector fixtures and the new DMA fixture rerun on the final source. Payload, SDK, ABI, source pin, smoke and all other lots unchanged; no physical gameplay, device allocation or FPS claim.",
